  "pages": [
    {
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "intro",
          "paragraphs": [
            "On the **LGV Méditerranée** (Avignon TGV included) there are no lineside signals: **TVM 430** shows the speed for each block in the cab, and the track carries only block marker boards. On the classic line into **Marseille Saint-Charles** the lineside **signaux** apply, with **KVB** checking speeds and stops and the **crocodile** repeating warning signals in the cab. The **VACMA** checks that you are awake. Speeds are in km/h. Quadrant controls are from TheJAG's TGV Duplex profile."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "systems",
          "title": "Safety systems",
          "cols": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "TVM 430",
              "full": "Transmission Voie-Machine",
              "summary": "Cab signalling through the rails. White on green = line speed; black on a **white diamond** = reach this speed by the next marker; white on **black** = applies now; **flashing** = a further reduction follows. Overspeed brakes the train.",
              "where": "LGV Méditerranée",
              "quadrant": "Left aux square = KVB, crocodile and TVM to Normal"
            },
            {
              "name": "KVB",
              "full": "Contrôle de Vitesse par Balises",
              "summary": "Beacons check the speed to stop signals and limits against a braking curve: an alert 5 km/h over, then the brake. Display codes: **00 / 000** stop ahead, **P / L** limits, **FU** it has braked.",
              "where": "In and around Marseille",
              "quadrant": "Left aux square = KVB, crocodile and TVM to Normal"
            },
            {
              "name": "Crocodile",
              "full": "Répétition des signaux (RS)",
              "summary": "A contact ramp at warning signals. Closed-signal warning: the alert lamp flashes (with a bip); press **Acknowledge**; it stays lit until you pass the signal. Open signal: a tone only. Real world: 5 s, then the brake.",
              "where": "Classic line into Marseille",
              "quadrant": "**Gear lever** = Acknowledge; left aux square = KVB, crocodile and TVM to Normal"
            },
            {
              "name": "VACMA",
              "full": "Veille Automatique à Contrôle de Maintien d'Appui",
              "summary": "Real: hold the pedal; release and press again when the buzzer asks. **In TSW**: above 8 km/h a buzzer every 60 s; press Acknowledge within 5 s or the emergency brake applies.",
              "where": "Every SNCF train",
              "quadrant": "**Gear lever** = Acknowledge; right aux square = VACMA to Normal"
            }
          ]
        },
